   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. The stereocentres are assigned by assumption, not read from the wedges, and two counts are judgement calls.\n\n**Fatty-acid tail.** An octadecanedioic acid (C18 diacid) is acylated onto the \u03b1-amine of a \u03b3-Glu. The \u03b3-carboxyl of the Glu is linked through two 8-amino-3,6-dioxaoctanoic acid (PEG-type) spacers to the \u03b5-amine of a Lys.\n\n**Main peptide chain** (from the Lys side, reading toward the ring):\n- Lys-NH2 (C-terminal primary amide)\n- Sarcosine (N-methylglycine)\n- 3-pyridylalanine\n- Asn\n- Glu (free side-chain acid)\n- 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid (a quaternary THP residue)\n- 2-naphthylalanine\n- Tyr with its phenol O-alkylated as OCH2CH2NH2\n\n**Macrocycle.** Penicillamine (Pen) is C(CH3)2 attached to S, so the two Pen residues are joined by a disulfide. The ring runs Pen \u2013 Lys(\u03b5-NHAc) \u2013 7-methyl-Trp \u2013 Thr \u2013 Asn \u2013 Pen\u2032. Pen\u2032 carries an N-terminal Ac-Lys(\u03b5-NMe3\u207a).\n\n**Judgement calls:**\n- The diacid is taken as 16 CH2 plus the two carbonyl carbons (the chain was not counted vertex by vertex).\n- The trimethylated Lys side chain is taken as 4 CH2 between the \u03b1-carbon and N\u207a.\n- All stereocentres are written as the L-amino-acid configuration. This includes the Nal, Pen and Pen\u2032 residues, where the hashed bonds were hard to read.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)O)CCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)CN(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1cccnc1)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)O)NC(=O)C1(CCOCC1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)(C)S%10)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1c[nH]c2c(C)cccc12)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@H](CCCC[N+](C)(C)C)NC(C)=O)C(C)(C)S%10"
